NNAAMMEE
     aauuttoommoouunntt — update autofs mounts

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aauuttoommoouunntt [--DD _n_a_m_e_=_v_a_l_u_e] [--LL] [--cc] [--ff] [--oo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [--vv] [--uu]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     When called without options, the aauuttoommoouunntt command parses the
     auto_master(5) configuration file and any direct maps that it references,
     and mounts or unmounts autofs(5) filesystems to match.  These options are
     available:

     --DD  Define a variable.  It is only useful with --LL.

     --LL  Do not mount or unmount anything.  Instead parse auto_master(5) and
         any direct maps, then print them to standard output.  When specified
         more than once, all the maps, including indirect ones, will be parsed
         and shown.  This is useful when debugging configuration problems.

     --cc  Flush caches, discarding possibly stale information obtained from
         maps and directory services.

     --ff  Force unmount, to be used with --uu.

     --oo  Specify mount options to be used along with the ones specified in the
         maps.  It is only useful with --LL.

     --uu  Try to unmount filesystems mounted by automountd(8).  autofs(5)
         mounts are not unmounted.  To unmount all autofs mounts, use uummoouunntt
         --AAtt aauuttooffss.

     --vv  Increase verbosity.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The aauuttoommoouunntt utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Unmount all filesystems mounted by automountd(8):
           aauuttoommoouunntt --uu

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     auto_master(5), autofs(5), automountd(8), autounmountd(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aauuttoommoouunntt command appeared in FreeBSD 10.1.

